  "decision_rule": "A gate cell missing either of its two bars reads VOID_ANCHOR_FAILED and voids the sweep. A baseline at or above 0.6134114 reads VOID_CONTROL_FAILED and voids the sweep. Otherwise, no checkpoint reaching the formed threshold reads NOT_FORMED_BY_FINAL, treated as an instrument fault. Otherwise the stability test decides: inside both ranges reads FORMED_EARLY_AND_HELD when the formation step is at or before step16000 and FORMED_LATE_AND_HELD when it is later; outside either range with the movement running one way in steps reads FORMED_AND_DRIFTED; outside either range and not one-way reads UNSTABLE_NOT_CLASSIFIABLE, which is the stability test's own committed name for that outcome. If neither channel yields a range at all the stability test reads HOLD_TEST_NOT_COMPUTABLE, which twelve measured checkpoints cannot produce and which is named here rather than left to be invented later.",
